        "original_id": "9b0a7019-e849-5b75-bdd5-0298530eaed6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Batman (1989 film), \"Batdance\"\n- People: Tim Burton, Jon Peters, Peter Guber, Prince\n- Companies: DC Comics, Mandalay Entertainment\n- Roles: Chairman, CEO\n- Topics: American superhero films, American music charts\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, Prince's song \"Kiss\" was the last of his songs before \"Batdance\" to top all three American charts.\n- In 1989, Batman was released as an American superhero film based on the DC Comics character Batman.\n- In 1989, Batman was directed by Tim Burton and produced by Jon Peters and Peter Guber.\n- Helped by the popularity of the 1989 film Batman, Prince's song \"Batdance\" reached number one in the United States.\n- \"Batdance\" became Prince's fourth American number-one single and his first since 1986 to top all three American charts.\n- Peter Guber is Chairman and CEO of Mandalay Entertainment.",
